{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age","id":42904,"title":"What are the options for Mages not dying of old age?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-05T08:46:56-08:00","id":42904,"title":"What are the options for Mages not dying of old age?","content":"Hey I'm less savvy on Awakening Rules compared to Ascension, but what are the various methods that Mages use to not die of old Age.<br /> <br /> Was it you stop worrying about age as an Archmage, or was it just you're eternal on your Golden Road?<br /> <br /> Would not switching bodies with younger people also work to stave off death, but how easy is that?<br /> <br /> I remember before Death can extend one's life, irony.<br /> <br /> Couldn't you use the Life Arcana to just make yourself younger? Or is that not possible as it is only temporary or something?<br /> <br /> I'm assuming we had artifacts and items/places that extended life throughout the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:57:59-08:00","id":42910,"title":"","content":"Death 5+Life 3 lets you put yourself in someone else's body (and eject their soul, sucks to be them). Life 5+Death 4 lets you dramatically slow your aging, with exceptional success stopping your aging entirely. Life 3 has a spell that (among other things) adds 25 years per Life dot to your lifespan. Archmastery of any arcana gives you the ability to become immortal, but those are imperial spells so you have to get creative on your own for those. You could also likely get creative with Time and/or Fate at &lt;6 dots to extend your life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T09:01:05-08:00","id":42915,"title":"","content":"Could a mage put themselves into a constructed body, or an artifact body, a robot body, or a tree/animal body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T09:04:59-08:00","id":42916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=42915#post42915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a mage</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. With the right arcana, anything is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T09:14:49-08:00","id":42921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgmoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=42916#post42916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes. With the right arcana, anything is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay replace that question then with what Arcana could a mage...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:03:12-08:00","id":42950,"title":"","content":"For a construct body, you'd need Matter 5 (to make the body; see the homunculus stuff in TotM), then Death 5+Life 3 at least (using a version of Steal Body). You might also need Life 5 to make the body actually animate, depending on interpretation. I would say not, personally. A robot body would likely be much the same, possibly with Forces 3-4 depending on how Iron Man you wanna be. For an artifact I would say at least Prime 4, likely 5, as well as a significant effort involved with finding the freaking artifact body. For an animal or plant body, simply use Steal Body above, or a variant thereof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T12:02:11-08:00","id":43050,"title":"","content":"How attached are you to your current form? I mean, you could hang around as a ghost mage, there's a legacy in Sublime which allows a third level member to become a spirit at death, or you could become a morphean from Astral Realms.<br /> <br /> They're all kinda life extensions... well, you continue to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:46:37-08:00","id":43181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=43050#post43050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How attached are you to your current form? I mean, you could hang around as a ghost mage, there's a legacy in Sublime which allows a third level member to become a spirit at death, or you could become a morphean from Astral Realms.<br /> <br /> They're all kinda life extensions... well, you continue to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, your friendly neighbourhood Tremere Lich would just <i>love </i>for you to drop by! For a chat! None of this 'wait until your dead with diminished powers' rubbish - just sign here on the dotted line. It's not like you were really <i>using </i>your soul, anyway ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1896-winnersh-3","name":"Winnersh 3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1896_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T17:20:15-08:00","id":43236,"title":"","content":"Just about every method of immortality that isn't an imperial spell usually has bad and risky side effects. Most immortal mages are declared Liches, and hunted. Mage society tends to be twitchy and nervous around those immortals, just in case said mages are doing something dark and unnatural to stay healthy and alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T17:55:49-08:00","id":43250,"title":"","content":"theres an artifact in the Arrows book that makes you inmortal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T20:07:08-08:00","id":43301,"title":"","content":"So are the Vast vast majority of mages then never going to use magic to extend their life? In the CWOD it was common that Masters extended their Life, and Archmages used a lot of tricks. Is the NWOD Mage assuming most mages won't try to use their own powers/barter for extended life unless they are being drastic, or becoming Archmages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T20:51:25-08:00","id":43323,"title":"","content":"There's also the Steal Lifespan rote from the core book that lets you just take a few years off random sleepers using Death 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1764-cesario","name":"Cesario","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T21:20:08-08:00","id":43336,"title":"","content":"The thing with Mage (either Ascension or Awakening) was to use your Spheres/Arcanum creatively. You can look through the main book and you could think up combinations that no one else has. So you should delve into things and start seeing what you can come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T21:57:21-08:00","id":43350,"title":"","content":"You can also make deals with Abyssal or Supernal (or other) entities for a respite from aging. Core rulebook has it in the Acamoth Investments. Summoners has it in the Fortification category of requests you can ask for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T22:16:26-08:00","id":43353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=43301#post43301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are the Vast vast majority of mages then never going to use magic to extend their life? In the CWOD it was common that Masters extended their Life, and Archmages used a lot of tricks. Is the NWOD Mage assuming most mages won't try to use their own powers/barter for extended life unless they are being drastic, or becoming Archmages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Atlantean mages do have something of a bias against efforts to cheat death. While using Life to extend the lifespan by a century or so is not generally looked down upon, outright immortality tends to get viewed by orthodoxy as a violation of the natural order based on beliefs regarding Stygia. Which of course doesn't stop enterprising Free Councilors (who are decidedly more accepting of liches and such things in general by way of comparison) and Left-Handed mages from investing in such things to varying degrees.<br /> <br /> And of course, once you become an Archmaster it becomes a comparatively simple matter, but then at that point you're violating the normal boundaries of Awakened magic anyway and so it's not a very useful point for discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T03:11:53-08:00","id":43418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So are the Vast vast majority of mages then never going to use magic to extend their life? </div> </div> </div>It seems implied, but I don't think it's overtly stated. That said, it's never really stated what the limits of Life magic and mana healing are, so it's possible that even discounting life-extension magic and baring death by misadventure, a mage could have a very long life expectancy anyway, maybe 120 years through simply having supernaturally effective healthcare.<br /> <br /> That's before getting into any of the metaphysics of people being fated to die or magical growth stagnating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the CWOD it was common that Masters extended their Life, and Archmages used a lot of tricks. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd imagine the de-emphasis of immortal magi is to remove the top-heavy social structure, which is what I believe the Avatar Storm was intended to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T03:39:47-08:00","id":43425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=43301#post43301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are the Vast vast majority of mages then never going to use magic to extend their life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most are unlikely to become powerful enough to try in the first place.<br /> <br /> For all the taboos against Liches, I'd say it's more likely that many mages don't pursue magics that can extend their life because they're too busy obsessing over some other thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T04:05:05-08:00","id":43430,"title":"","content":"The vast majority of mages aren't going to try to live past old age. That said, &quot;old age&quot; for a mage is quite a lot older than it is for a Sleeper, because any Thyrsus, mage with a Thyrsus in their cabal, or other mage with a middling amount of Life will never suffer from long-term diseases and physical conditions. &quot;Natural lifespan&quot; for mages is around 90-100.<br /> <br /> Some mages use Life magic to push on past that, but the body has limits. To live past 130-ish, you're looking at <i>alternatives</i>. Most of which involve screwing someone else in the process or giving up your humanity, and are thus decried as lichdom.<br /> <br /> Socially, mages don't go for immortality (even most archmasters don't!), because the common means of doing so are, as you'd expect, in the Death Arcanum's purview. And Moros are predisposed to <i>accepting</i> death as a transformative state, not fighting it.<br /> <br /> The Free Council goes easier on liches than other orders because they didn't have the tussle with the Tremere the Diamond did in the middle ages, because thanks to that tussle lichdom is seen as Left-Handed so most research into it went on in the Nameless orders - some sects that went on to join the Free Council were originally kicked out by the Diamond for being overly interested in it - and because during the desperation of the Great Refusal, many of the oldest and most powerful Nameless (who were reaching the end of their useful lifespan after being among the big population boom in Nameless in the 19th Century) took to looking at Seers of the Throne's souls and bodies as the spoils of war. <i>Steal Body</i> was a terror weapon and a way for the LIbertine generals to carry on into the 20th Century.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 01-06-2014, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T10:07:33-08:00","id":43586,"title":"","content":"Very Interesting. Yeah I assumed the super health care perk would get most mages to live long just by avoiding basic disease anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:35:16-08:00","id":44316,"title":"","content":"How much life would a high level Prime mage need to replace portions of their body with phantasms? Something along the lines of Create Complex Phantasm or Create Tulpa but designed to produce a replacement for the body that could still hold the soul of the mage.<br /> How vulnerable would such a thing be to dispelling?<br /> If it worked, would the mage be able to use their own Prime magic to do things like turn into a bird without Life by altering the phantasm or giving themselves wings? <br /> Could the mage do things like given themselves wings on a temporary or permanent basis using Prime for just the phantasm or would they need Life because it would be stuck to their body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:04:19-08:00","id":44347,"title":"","content":"I would think at least 4, maybe 5. It would be as vulnerable as any ongoing spell, so you'd definitely want to relinquish it with a WP dot so as to protect against that. You would also likely need to have Death at considerable levels to transfer your soul to the phantasmal body, although it could be argued that with Prime 5 (plus some value of Life, at least 3) you could cast a spell to turn your soul <i>into</i> a complex phantasm, at which point you'd be an entirely Prime-based life form. Which sounds kind of awesome.<br /> <br /> Now, if you'll excuse me, I have an email to send my ST. &lt;.&lt;;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:18:28-08:00","id":44358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgmoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=44347#post44347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think at least 4, maybe 5. It would be as vulnerable as any ongoing spell, so you'd definitely want to relinquish it with a WP dot so as to protect against that. You would also likely need to have Death at considerable levels to transfer your soul to the phantasmal body, although it could be argued that with Prime 5 (plus some value of Life, at least 3) you could cast a spell to turn your soul <i>into</i> a complex phantasm, at which point you'd be an entirely Prime-based life form. Which sounds kind of awesome.<br /> <br /> Now, if you'll excuse me, I have an email to send my ST. &lt;.&lt;;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're overestimating things. You would need Life in order to feel with the Phantasmal prosthetic, but there's no need to transfer your soul into it. Even with just Prime, a complex phantasm can be used as a perfectly functional prosthetic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> although it could be argued that with Prime 5 (plus some value of Life, at least 3) you could cast a spell to turn your soul <i>into</i> a complex phantasm, at which point you'd be an entirely Prime-based life form. Which sounds kind of awesome. </div> </div> </div>The soul is DEATH's purview. This would be a Prime/Death spell. And first of all, you'd need to come up with a Death/Space spell that allows your soul to exist outside your body without you suffering the effects of soullessness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=44316#post44316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much life would a high level Prime mage need to replace portions of their body with phantasms? Something along the lines of Create Complex Phantasm or Create Tulpa but designed to produce a replacement for the body that could still hold the soul of the mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why you would care about whether or not it holds your soul.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How vulnerable would such a thing be to dispelling? </div> </div> </div>Just as vulnerable as any other spell. If it has a high potency, not very.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it worked, would the mage be able to use their own Prime magic to do things like turn into a bird without Life by altering the phantasm or giving themselves wings? </div> </div> </div>You could create a phantasmal suit around yourself that gives you giant wings, or the form of a giant bird, but you can't shrink yourself without Life. Your body has to fit inside of whatever phantasm you make if you want to do this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could the mage do things like given themselves wings on a temporary or permanent basis using Prime for just the phantasm or would they need Life because it would be stuck to their body? </div> </div> </div>Just Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 01-07-2014, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:32:04-08:00","id":44365,"title":"","content":"The soul is also Prime's purview, as seen in Supernal Vision's auspex-style effect, various aura-meddling effects, and Armor of the Soul. You would certainly not need Space to be a freed soul, as that has nothing to do with correspondences and sympathetic connections. You do, however, need Life to make something living. If you just want a prosthetic you could do it with Prime, but you would have to concentrate on the damn thing <i>every time you wanted to move</i>. To function as a body, you would need Life; probably 5 dots to create an Animate Homunculus style effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:45:48-08:00","id":44369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgmoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=44365#post44365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The soul is also Prime's purview, as seen in Supernal Vision's auspex-style effect, various aura-meddling effects, and Armor of the Soul. You would certainly not need Space to be a freed soul, as that has nothing to do with correspondences and sympathetic connections. You do, however, need Life to make something living. If you just want a prosthetic you could do it with Prime, but you would have to concentrate on the damn thing <i>every time you wanted to move</i>. To function as a body, you would need Life; probably 5 dots to create an Animate Homunculus style effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the subtle arcana have spells dealing with the Soul. Death binds it, Fate frees it, Spirit restores it, Prime protects it, and Mind shapes it. Death, however, is the only Arcana to explicitly list the Soul as its purview.<br /> <br /> You would need Space together with Death in order to maintain the link between one's soul and body even while the two are separated.<br /> <br /> You would need Death and Mind in order to exist as an ephemeral soul-entity, because your soul alone does not have a mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 01-07-2014, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T15:59:00-08:00","id":45895,"title":"","content":"See? all this talk about what you need to fully, functionally, remove your soul.. about whether or not you can feel in a false body.. about what arcana has power over the soul (check out left handed path for that answer)..? Thats lichdom. All those sorts of spells would get you Nameless and banned very quickly. Mucking with your soul that thoroughly, without knowing the side effects, will be considered lichdom by most Councils. Granted, that isn't saying it can't be done, or that it wouldn't work.. just that it will earn you mistrust to try, or ask anyone for help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T20:35:42-08:00","id":46024,"title":"","content":"Actually, you're mistaking the terms here. Left-Hand Path defines those who make a practice of fiddling with the soul as 'Reapers'. Liches are mages who extend their lives at the expense of others.<br /> <br /> The two terms are often conflated because the most successful academic lineage for both varieties of illicit sorcery is the Tremere.<br /> <br /> And the reasons I could see most archmasters wanting to make themselves immortal amount to:<br /> <br /> 1) Making an ideological point (Aswadim who reject the limitations of reality anyway, Silver Ladder Exemplars who believe limited lifespans are a symptom of the Lie, etc.)<br /> <br /> 2) Feeling like their goals are taking too long, or that they achieved the Imperial Mysteries too late in life to get by with the lifespan they have left to make any headway towards Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 01-09-2014, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T13:46:25-08:00","id":46466,"title":"","content":"Honestly, developer's statements or not, the notion most archmasters reject immortality is as utterly outlandish and implausible as most citizens of an industrialized nation forsaking the comforts of modern technology and medicine. An extremist fringe might do it, but the vast majority of the community is going to have much more pragmatic a viewpoint.<br /> <br /> This for various reasons: 1) there are plenty of ways Imperial magic may be used to gain immortality without harming anyone 2) by its godlike nature, archmastery already bestows a transhuman perspective 3) Path restrictions to Arcana are much less meaningful to archmasters, so they can master Death if they wish even if they aren't Moros; moreover several other Arcana may be used for immortality besides Death 4) immortality is not a violation of the Pax 5) archmasters may easily decide they need as much time as necessary to accomplish Ascension and their other various personal goals and plans for the Tellurian and they won't in all likelihood achieve them within a human lifespan 6) immortality may be an ideological statement for various kinds of archmasters 7) even for archmasters that believe in death as a transformative experience, it is very easy to reason out their current status is as much mystical/spiritual development as they are going to get this side of Ascension; in all likelihood, this is their final and most enlightened life unless they really, really screw up, so there is little spiritual gain or merit in waiting for another incarnation.<br /> <br /> To a less outlandish degree, the notion also defies credibility that the Diamond Orders would remain rather ideologically hostile to immortality because of a minor scuffle they had with the Tremere about a millennium ago. Especially since we are also expected to assume very few Diamond mages from that era remain alive to embody and enforce that viewpoint. On its own, time would have corroded that kind of bad blood to nothingness long ago. The lasting features of mage society that endure the ages like the phoenix typically do so because they have some Supernal entity actively supporting them, such as Exemplars propping up the Orders, the Exarchs propping up the Seers, and so on. There may certainly be some very-high-Wisdom mages that are entirely unwilling to screw up someone else (including various kinds of assholes) or give up their humanity for immortality, but just as surely they do not make up the vast majority of Awakened society or define its mainstream policy and ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-10-2014, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T15:38:57-08:00","id":46548,"title":"","content":"Firstly, archmasters don't age while on their Road. Because of this archmaster who mostly use proxies and spend most of their time on their Road (or in their Chantry) don't need to research immortality.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I don't think the developers ever said anything about archmasters rejecting immortality. Even one of the example characters is an immortal (and has been for a long time). The biggest reason for archmages not to become immortal for them is to retain some semblance of humanity and mortality. But as long as they don't really care about that and have need for it, immortality is fair game as most of them are already somewhat transhumanist.<br /> <br /> Normal mages do have a taboo on immortality, but that is mostly because of their historical clash with the Tremere and the fact that most methods are really immoral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T16:28:14-08:00","id":46577,"title":"","content":"IIRC DaveB said that the Mages that did reject immortality through archmastery did so because crossing the Abyss and screwing around with the Telurian is just too damned scary (risking being eaten by the abyss or totally erased from every possible reality ever because of one mistake in the arrangement of Supernal Symbols), or because they didn't want to go from being the top &quot;Big Fish In A Small Pond&quot; to &quot;Nemo in the ocean full of Big Boys&quot;, they'll stay here where they have money, power, adoring followers, apprentices that owe them ALL the favors and all the drugs they'll ever need thankyouverymuch.<br /> <br /> Which, I gotta say, sounds like a pretty convincing argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-10-2014, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T17:12:49-08:00","id":46600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=46466#post46466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An extremist fringe might do it, but the vast majority of the community is going to have much more pragmatic a viewpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmasters are not generally pragmatists. Archmasters are generally extremist mystics and ideologues who exist within a cosmology and emerge from a society that generally stigmatizes evading death.<br /> <br /> And a whole bunch of other things that Imperial spells are technically capable of; despite the practices of Entity and Excision, archmasters are unlikely to transmute themselves into weird transhuman conglomerates of indestructible substance and metaphysically removed vulnerabilities, because of the motivations that drive one into archmastery and the quintessences likely involved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To a less outlandish degree, the notion also defies credibility that the Diamond Orders would remain rather ideologically hostile to immortality because of a minor scuffle they had with the Tremere about a millennium ago. Especially since we are also expected to assume very few Diamond mages from that era remain alive to embody and enforce that viewpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know why Catholicism practices clerical chastity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T17:22:13-08:00","id":46608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=44316#post44316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much life would a high level Prime mage need to replace portions of their body with phantasms? Something along the lines of Create Complex Phantasm or Create Tulpa but designed to produce a replacement for the body that could still hold the soul of the mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the concept of patterns in the setting, I'd say there's a limit to the degree that Practices other than Entities can mess around with the fundamentals of how a body works before it stops metaphysically qualifying as a body, and thus loses some of the desired qualities.<br /> <br /> Like, the metaphysical connection between body, mind and soul is probably kind of numinous and vague to mages, with Steal Body being one of the few ways to overcome it (and one that still leaves you in a human body).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T18:24:11-08:00","id":46648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=46600#post46600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archmasters are not generally pragmatists. Archmasters are generally extremist mystics and ideologues who exist within a cosmology and emerge from a society that generally stigmatizes evading death.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) the typical mystical and ideological reasons a mage may seek archmastery are not ones closely tied to acceptance of death, quite the contrary 2) to a good degree, archmastery is tied to a transhumanist perspective 3) many ideological or ethical reasons that may lead a mage to forsake immortality become obsolete with archmastery: Imperial magic makes it trivial to become immortal without harming no one; there seems to be very little mystical and spiritual point in further reincarnation when archmastery is achieved - the only way to progress further appears Ascension.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a whole bunch of other things that Imperial spells are technically capable of; despite the practices of Entity and Excision, archmasters are unlikely to transmute themselves into weird transhuman conglomerates of indestructible substance and metaphysically removed vulnerabilities, because of the motivations that drive one into archmastery and the quintessences likely involved. </div> </div> </div>There are many possible ways the practices of Entity and Excision from several Arcana may bestow immortality, and as Imperial magic typically goes, it seems quite a vanilla feat, on the same scale as creating a sub-soul. This in all likelihood means many different quintessence options. An unlimited lifespan may well be an ideological statement, and even if it doesn't, it means unlimited time to achieve Ascension, your vision of mystical perfection, and/or your plans for the Tellurian, so it is a pragmatic means to your ideological agenda.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you know why Catholicism practices clerical chastity? </div> </div> </div>How many modern Catholics live like Middle Age monks ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-10-2014, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T18:58:45-08:00","id":46669,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, that Irioth, he keeps sneaking up on ya.<br /> <br /> Did prompt an interesting little summary of Nietzschean ideas once. Think I'd have more fun rereading that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many modern Catholics live like Middle Age monks ?</div> </div> </div> </div>.... The number of priests who don't marry?<br /> <br /> Now that that's cleared up, do you know why priests were forbidden from marriage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-10-2014, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T20:35:33-08:00","id":46712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=46669#post46669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did prompt an interesting little summary of Nietzschean ideas once. Think I'd have more fun rereading that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have my blessing, but hasn't the old forum's material got lost with the transition ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> .... The number of priests who don't marry?<br /> <br /> Now that that's cleared up, do you know why priests were forbidden from marriage? </div> </div> </div>I know those reasons (issues about keeping the Church's wealth in the hands of the clergy and affirming its political independence from secular authorities) but IMO the point is wholly irrelevant to our argument. As I see it, a much more correct comparison in this field to the attitudes of modern mage society about the heritage of a mllennium-old minor conflict is how many Christians in the Western world still live according to Middle Ages ideology and morality, and how much those ideas still define the policies of Western nations. Or for a slightly different analogy, how much the attitudes and policies of European and Arab people towards Asian people are defined by the Mongol invasions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-11-2014, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T02:55:35-08:00","id":46814,"title":"","content":"Mongols don't drain people's souls, and looking on wikipedia will give you a reasonable overview of the military might of Mongolia. Neither of those is true of the Tremere.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'm not sure if this applies to archmasters, and actually I'm not sure why they'd need to. They already look pretty immortal as it is. Their bigger problem seems to be finding new sources of arcane XP. Immortality is pretty irrelevant if all the incredibly obsessive magician can do is stagnate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T17:34:46-08:00","id":47145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=46814#post46814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their bigger problem seems to be finding new sources of arcane XP. Immortality is pretty irrelevant if all the incredibly obsessive magician can do is stagnate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psst: Astral stipulations on earned experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T03:48:44-08:00","id":47316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=46712#post46712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how many Christians in the Western world still live according to Middle Ages ideology and morality, and how much those ideas still define the policies of Western nations.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://kinialohaguy.files.wordpress.com/2010/06/banghead.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I blame myself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T06:22:32-08:00","id":47345,"title":"","content":"Arguments about harming people fail to apply any longer once you are working with Imperial Magic. Every change you make to the cosmos through your own alterations in the Supernal is arguably harming an indefinable number of people who now no longer exist, now never existed, or who have now been harmed/killed/etc... because of Butterfly Effect style ripples through the fabric of reality. If those people are more important than whatever you want, you'd better just give up, now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1768-demdemeh","name":"Demdemeh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T06:48:18-08:00","id":47357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=47316#post47316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I blame myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be a bit more loquacious: I think Isator's point was that priests are still forbidden from marriage, even though the original reason is far removed. Similarly, mage society can retain a taboo against immortality even though the original event that spurred it was centuries ago. Once something has entered a culture, it is possible for it to stay there for quite some time, and the four Atlantean orders value tradition.<br /> <br /> This, of course, ignores the fact that Tremere liches are still a thing that exists right now, and watching people for signs of lichdom is the kind of thing that Guardians of the Veil do right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T07:12:02-08:00","id":47370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=46608#post46608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the concept of patterns in the setting, I'd say there's a limit to the degree that Practices other than Entities can mess around with the fundamentals of how a body works before it stops metaphysically qualifying as a body, and thus loses some of the desired qualities.<br /> <br /> Like, the metaphysical connection between body, mind and soul is probably kind of numinous and vague to mages, with Steal Body being one of the few ways to overcome it (and one that still leaves you in a human body).</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider the fact that you no longer have a body when when in your golden road. Also, how Siddha tend to leave their human forms. It's entirely possible that bodies are completely optional to archmasters even ones that don't have sufficient mastery over life using the arcana in nature because they are altering the vessels that gives them form when they go to the fallen world similar to how planeswalkers used to work in Magic the gathering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T03:15:07-08:00","id":48039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=46600#post46600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know why Catholicism practices clerical chastity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it helped reinforce Rome's control of the Church by ending dynastic priestly families that were causing local difficulties, and simplified Church financing of priests by removing concerns with how to deal with wives/children. Which is to say, it was administrative wrangling given a veneer of religious fol-de-rol to justify it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T03:19:54-08:00","id":48043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=47316#post47316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"http://kinialohaguy.files.wordpress.com/2010/06/banghead.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I blame myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe he means christian ethos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T03:34:15-08:00","id":48048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=47357#post47357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be a bit more loquacious: I think Isator's point was that priests are still forbidden from marriage, even though the original reason is far removed. Similarly, mage society can retain a taboo against immortality even though the original event that spurred it was centuries ago. Once something has entered a culture, it is possible for it to stay there for quite some time, and the four Atlantean orders value tradition.<br /> <br /> This, of course, ignores the fact that Tremere liches are still a thing that exists right now, and watching people for signs of lichdom is the kind of thing that Guardians of the Veil do right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, mages tend to be rather individualistic, since the Consilium structure is sort of a herding meglomanical cats deal, not Magic Uber Alles fascism. That the Tremere got it glaringly wrong is no reason for all mages to just throw their hands in the air and refuse to explore immortality. After all, just look at the dearth of banks that resulted after the first bank robbery; we have laws against setting up banks precisely because they spawn bank robbers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Tremere are soul-stealing jerks. Of course you go after them. But to reject all attempts to use magic to achieve immortality because they failed - even as spectacularly as they failed - seems short-sighted. Unless mages lose a fairly basic human response to failure, i.e. &quot;that blew up spectacularly; let's try it again but this time we come up with a method that doesn't involve flaming wreckage&quot;, the idea that they just refuse to try is ludicrous (that they may not be able to actually succeed is not ludicrous, but the idea that they all just refuse is).<br /> <br /> Also, Alexander VI took clerical chastity out behind the vestry and rogered it silly - and the current kiddie-diddling problems suggests enough breech than observance to effectively nullify the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T03:37:34-08:00","id":48049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=46600#post46600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know why Catholicism practices clerical chastity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because one of the prerequisites is loving God before anyone else.<br /> <br /> Probably some thing about difficulties with Nepotism too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T04:57:57-08:00","id":48074,"title":"","content":"The issue isn't some Catholic analogy. The issue is that the Path of Death is actually the Path of Transformation - Moros specialise in the Supernal resonance of transition between fixed states. The Path has always been portrayed as being curiously not-at-all morbid. Death, to the main researchers into it in Mage's universe, is a spiritual transition which isn't something to fear or put off forever. Delay, sure, but everything dies eventually. In-setting, the fear of death, and the related fear that only an elect few get to the afterlife <u>is one of the Exarchs</u>.<br /> <br /> Tremere believe differently, but they've had their spiritual nature dipped into the Abyss as part of their recruitment - they're a corrupted form of the Moros.<br /> <br /> Do other mages fear death and seek immortality? A few, but predominantly members of other Paths. The Pentacle takes the majority Moros lead because that's how Pentacle society works. The Silver Ladder know that morbid fear is one of the Enemy, and think that Ascension is preferable to lichdom (and that most lichdom methods corrupt the soul, so preclude Ascension). The further a group gets from the meritocratic &quot;listen to the experts&quot; core of mage society, the more accepting it is of fringe ideas like making your stay in the Fallen World permanent.<br /> <br /> Death Archmasters are, thanks to the way Archmastery works, mostly either ex-Moros or mages who had Death as a third Ruling Arcanum through their Legacy. The characters with the greatest ability to seek immortality methods are the ones with the least inclination to do it.<br /> <br /> Exceptions exist, and when we're talking about Masters and archmasters everyone's an exceptional individual, but they're on the fringes because a fifth of the Awakened - the important fifth to the subject - mostly reject immortality as a philosophy and decry it as a spiritually poisionous dead-end. That most liches <i>are</i> Mad, bad, or dangerous to know just reinforces that societal stereotype. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T06:46:53-08:00","id":48128,"title":"","content":"I still admit to having trouble, despite intellectual understanding, of why a Death Archmaster wouldn't just go 'well I'd rather not get killed before I Ascend' and then remove their ability to die despite those prior beliefs. If only out of a sense of self-preservation and an awareness of how hideously long it can take to achieve that goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T07:10:26-08:00","id":48142,"title":"","content":"Define &quot;I don't want to die&quot;. Archmasters don't age on their Roads or in the Supernal, and fixing your soul to the Fallen World to become immortal might <i>prevent</i> Ascension.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also &quot;not get killed&quot; and &quot;not age&quot; are two different things. Vampires, for example, are quite easily killable. When you're a Death-8 posthuman spider sitting in a web of magical and personal influence, acting through agents that come to you and avatar forms that don't risk your unaging self, deciding &quot;I'd best make it so I dont age&quot; is gilding the lilly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why go through the pain and uncertain transformation of Excising your ability to die when your perfect, adaptive mage armor shields you from all harm anyway?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 01-13-2014, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T08:34:12-08:00","id":48192,"title":"","content":"That and Excising your capacity to die probably just means that anybody who gets severely pissed off at you just seals you in a volcano for eternity.<br /> <br /> Or an abstraction, or a space between seconds, or some other horrifying thing that the kinds of magic archmasters contend against is capable of.<br /> <br /> Or they just go back in time to smother you in the crib.<br /> <br /> I am of course facetiously ignoring the relevance of quintessences in these procedures, but then, so do most discussions of excessive personal transformation magic, so fair game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:45:13-08:00","id":48250,"title":"","content":"If you can't get something done with ultimate cosmic power in the six score years a Mage gets you really didn't want it anyways. Get busy livin', or get busy dyin'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:45:47-08:00","id":48254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=48192#post48192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they just go back in time to smother you in the crib.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that would work to kill an Archmaster - in the same way that going back in time and making your parents never meet results in the world proceeding as though you never existed, yet you remain alive despite that fact. Archmastery seems to anchor you in existance in a way that makes you semi-immune to timeline tampering.<br /> <br /> Or something. Maybe it's different because they're actually damaging you instead of loop-holing you out of existence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T16:33:29-08:00","id":48569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=48142#post48142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define &quot;I don't want to die&quot;. Archmasters don't age on their Roads or in the Supernal, and fixing your soul to the Fallen World to become immortal might <i>prevent</i> Ascension.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also &quot;not get killed&quot; and &quot;not age&quot; are two different things. Vampires, for example, are quite easily killable. When you're a Death-8 posthuman spider sitting in a web of magical and personal influence, acting through agents that come to you and avatar forms that don't risk your unaging self, deciding &quot;I'd best make it so I dont age&quot; is gilding the lilly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why go through the pain and uncertain transformation of Excising your ability to die when your perfect, adaptive mage armor shields you from all harm anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>(I didn't want to quote something else so this is to your first post) The problem with golden roads though is that without a chantry, it's a very boring place to live. It's a place of solitude which might be nice for some but it would make others go insane in a short time period. Not everyone who became an archmaster did so by remaining in solitude and contemplating their navel. For the most part, it seems like Archmages wouldn't want to be in their Golden roads unless they want to sleep or meditate.<br /> <br /> So what about Siddha who naturally divest their bodies and alter their golden roads just to be more in tune with their element? Don't they become immortal as a side effect of becoming a being of pure electricity? What makes that better than a person who just can't age?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T16:36:43-08:00","id":48574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=48254#post48254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that would work to kill an Archmaster - in the same way that going back in time and making your parents never meet results in the world proceeding as though you never existed, yet you remain alive despite that fact. Archmastery seems to anchor you in existance in a way that makes you semi-immune to timeline tampering.<br /> <br /> Or something. Maybe it's different because they're actually damaging you instead of loop-holing you out of existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>No the rule is pretty clear. You can't just kill an archmaster before he was an archmaster. All that means is that you've possibly done him a favor and no one remembers who he was because he technically doesn't exist but he does. His act fundamentally altering of the cosmos for power trumps what the cosmos might say about his state of living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 01-13-2014, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:03:02-08:00","id":71302,"title":"","content":"So I got a question what about regular uses of various spells to retard the aging process? Like every time the mage sleeps they sleep in some sort of suspended animation so their body doesn't age, but they are replenished like they sleep. Or they regularly suspend their body when they do things like astral travel, or project their consciousness? For instance if a Seer makes regular use of a Profane Urim to possess bodies can't they find a way to keep their real self from aging?<br /> <br /> This was prevented in Mage the Ascension because Paradox was kind of more of a stickler their, but it seems kosher for Awakening. Why can't you just freeze your body in time and spend your consciousness outside it or in another body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:07:32-08:00","id":71311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=48569#post48569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I didn't want to quote something else so this is to your first post) The problem with golden roads though is that without a chantry, it's a very boring place to live. It's a place of solitude which might be nice for some but it would make others go insane in a short time period. Not everyone who became an archmaster did so by remaining in solitude and contemplating their navel. For the most part, it seems like Archmages wouldn't want to be in their Golden roads unless they want to sleep or meditate.<br /> <br /> So what about Siddha who naturally divest their bodies and alter their golden roads just to be more in tune with their element? Don't they become immortal as a side effect of becoming a being of pure electricity? What makes that better than a person who just can't age?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not necessarily boring, you can have visitors and other residents. And its a very groovy place to cast spells, which makes it a cool laboratory. And the whole Astral Travel Thing doesn't get boring quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:01:54-08:00","id":71599,"title":"","content":"I've always wondered why Steal Body was a Life spell and not a Mind spell. I understand including Death in order to handle the soul but I wonder if anyone has ideas about this. Does it make sense for someone with no other power over consciousness to take over a body? What exactly is the Life component of this spell and would a Mind/Death variant be workable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2122-montuban","name":"Montuban","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T02:52:23-08:00","id":71883,"title":"","content":"I also needed a bit stronger reason against long-lived mages than a cultural bias, so what I've done is to link it directly to wisdom.<br /> For every decade above 100 years, the mage suffers a wisdom breaking point.<br /> For every year above 150 years, the mage suffers a wisdom breaking point.<br /> For ever month over 200 years, the mage suffers a wisdom breaking point.<br /> I haven't nailed down the wisdom ratings for the these breaking points, but I am thinking something like 7, 5, 2 or similar, so something like 5, 3, and 2 dice. So once a mage gets above 200, he or she starts to break down fast.<br /> <br /> It's mostly a versimilitude thing, as it is unlikely ever to be relevant for a player character or even beyond anything as background information for a npc - we're unlikely to ever have to make those wisdom checks. Still it makes sense to me and reinforces the cultural bias. A 250 year old mage is likely not a very stable person.<br /> <br /> As to why living for too long degrades wisdom...<br /> - Wisdom is partially about natural order and balance. Living too long can easily be seen as violating the natural order.<br /> - Wisdom is a weapon of the Exarchs against the Oracles and their followers. By preventing Pentacle mages from becoming too old and too powerful, they reinforce the prison.<br /> - Wisdom is a blessing from the Oracles. It forces the Seers to move on, so the Exarchs cannot have 1000 year old mages in their service, making the prison-wardens too powerful to fight.<br /> <br /> From a story perspective, I like to avoid having too many, too old and too powerful mages around. It just makes the setting fall apart, imo, or at least shifts the focus. Dealing with ancient, inscrutable and insane elders is a vampire thing, not a mage thing. IMO of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not sure about the Steal Body spell. To my mind it should be Death 5/Life 3/Mind 5 or something. You are affecting a body (Life), you are transferring a Soul (Death) and you are transferring a Mind (Mind). Maybe it was just to simplify things? It is really an expansion of the Mind 5 spell Possession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T06:54:47-08:00","id":71952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For every decade above 100 years, the mage suffers a wisdom breaking point. </div> </div> </div>Why? Normal people can live at least to 120.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also needed a bit stronger reason against long-lived mages than a cultural bias, so what I've done is to link it directly to wisdom. </div> </div> </div>A negative view of serial killers is hardly a cultural bias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T07:35:12-08:00","id":71965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=71952#post71952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A negative view of serial killers is hardly a cultural bias.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the idea that since one group failed in one way no one else should even try any other way is. Humans are problem-solving machines. Mages are presented as being even more-so. To actively deny that imperative can only be achieved by active cultural suppression of normal human activity. This isn't to say there is a way to live forever, but the idea people not only don't try, but actively police to make sure no one tries is absurd. After all, we all saw how all attempts at flight (and even really high jumping) was forbidden after the Hindenburg crash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T08:49:44-08:00","id":72001,"title":"","content":"Ah, when I wrote &quot;for each decade after 100&quot; it was mostly because it is a nice round number. Also, I kinda assumed that the mage would be living with full mental and physical fitness, which can easily be seen as unnatural.<br /> <br /> If serial murder was the only option for this, there would be no reason for these mechanics. You can simple brute-force it with Life, Death and possibly Mind - Create a body empty of mind and soul and occupy it. Use some of the Life spells from Grimoire of Griomoires, etc. Hell, use Spirit to enslave a spirit of youth, force it to keep you young or, y'know, bargain with it. Once you become a master, it's really not that hard to extend your lifespan. It's a lot easier if you throw ethics and wisdom to the wind and start devouring souls or life force, but that's cool, it's supposed to be tempting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T10:21:11-08:00","id":72054,"title":"","content":"@ Phalamir<br /> I agree. Don't know what your point is, but I agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once you become a master, it's really not that hard to extend your lifespan. </div> </div> </div>I don't agree. Aside from the Grimoire of Grimoire spell which is clearly supposed to be a very obscure spell, if the other options were really viable then why would there be so much focus on the serial murderer option? I think you're trying to solve a problem which doesn't need to exist, and I don't think it even actually solves anything. You just have a lot of crazy immortal magi in your setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T10:53:55-08:00","id":72078,"title":"","content":"Using the Free Council rote mentioned above and Life 5, I could create a new body and inhabit it. There are weaknesses, sure, I am kinda screwed if my body gets dispelled, but y'know... eternal life right there. Death 5 and Life 5. If I am a master anyway, that's not really that big an investment.<br /> <br /> Also, it should be possible doing something about aging through Life and the Perfecting practice.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is probably an &quot;agree to disagree&quot; area, I've read the same books as you and come to a different conclusion.<br /> <br /> As for lots of crazy immortal mages... the tendency of immortal mages to go insane would explain why there is a strong imperative to move on and die eventually. The Seers and the Pentacle would probably actually enforce this, taking out mages in their own ranks who become too old and too insane.<br /> <br /> Also, it's a more interesting situation for me:<br /> Choosing between almost certain insanity or a natural death is a choice.<br /> Choosing between indefinite life or natural death is not really a choice. You still run the risk of going away if someone dispels your body or whatever solution you are using, but once you are 300 you would be dead anyway, so no huge loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T12:21:39-08:00","id":72138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=72054#post72054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if the other options were really viable then why would there be so much focus on the serial murderer option?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume someone with no regard for the actual capabilities of the Arcana saw that serial murder options and decided they should be the only ways of prolonging life because that would oh so dramatic, and damn logic.<br /> There are <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default1192-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=77175\" target=\"_blank\">lots of ways</a> creative use of the arcana should be able to prolong life. People seeing the take over bodies spell and the legacy that prolongs life by eating souls and deciding that these should be the only ways that work because Drama! has lead to some ridiculous bending over backwards just to keep them unique.<br /> I'm all for stuff that leads to more interesting drama in a game, but the amount of work and screwing with the rules you have to do to keep the serial murderer options the only workable ones is just not worth what they add to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 02-14-2014, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T13:00:29-08:00","id":72160,"title":"","content":"Hey now, writing rules and fluff that go in completely different directions is a time-honored white wolf tradition! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T13:58:10-08:00","id":72205,"title":"","content":"I would assume it's because the authors thought players were adults who could work out that there are implied rules to the setting that aren't concretely set out because that would hinder the flow of the game. Indeed I know that, because the rules frequently say that.<br /> <br /> Also, that's some nice use of the quotes there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T14:53:43-08:00","id":72244,"title":"","content":"Well, presumably we are all adults here and apparently some of us prefer there to be a clear correlation between rules and fluff, even if others consider that unnecessary. I see nothing inherently more adult about one position compared to another. No one wants rules that hinder the flow of the game.<br /> <br /> Considering that one of the stated goals for Blood and Smoke and the Fallen World Chronicles is to have a more clear connection between rules, fluff and setting, I think it likely that others are experiencing a bit of a disconnect. I think some of the devs stated this somewhere in the process, can't recall when/where though.<br /> <br /> The tone of your post seems a little condescending. You pretty much imply that Joker and I aren't adults... which isn't very nice and a bit unnecessary. Is there really any need for that? Might be me reading too much into it, but so far this has been a good, productive discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T02:10:47-08:00","id":72525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suicide King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=72160#post72160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey now, writing rules and fluff that go in completely different directions is a time-honored white wolf tradition! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just like &quot;see page XX&quot;. Seriously though guys, let's please keep the condescension out of our replies, shall we? Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T16:08:16-08:00","id":73939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=71302#post71302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I got a question what about regular uses of various spells to retard the aging process? Like every time the mage sleeps they sleep in some sort of suspended animation so their body doesn't age, but they are replenished like they sleep. Or they regularly suspend their body when they do things like astral travel, or project their consciousness? For instance if a Seer makes regular use of a Profane Urim to possess bodies can't they find a way to keep their real self from aging?<br /> <br /> This was prevented in Mage the Ascension because Paradox was kind of more of a stickler their, but it seems kosher for Awakening. Why can't you just freeze your body in time and spend your consciousness outside it or in another body?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are these Methods kosher yay or nay?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T05:49:24-08:00","id":74216,"title":"","content":"I'll give a shot at summing up. Apologies in advance if I misrepresent someones' positions. That is not my intent.<br /> <br /> One position is that these method exists and are reasonable effective, they do not cause paradox (more so than normal) or wisdom loss. There is just a strong cultural bias against them among the mage community, coming from old conflicts with the Tremere. Also coming from the fact that the most effective, easiest and foolproof methods are essentially serial murder. If you prolong your life beyond the natural lifespan (with some leeway), you are associating with <i>those</i> people. You generally don't want that. Another factor is that the voices of authority on this (Moros) are strongly conditioned by their Path and Awakening to disapprove and disavow prolonging your life in general.<br /> <br /> I am kinda paraphrasing DaveB in this and this is likely the closest to a &quot;word of God&quot; ruling you are going to get. If you want to go with the &quot;official&quot; ruling, I'd say go with this. This stuff works, there are &quot;just&quot; social consequences for using them.<br /> <br /> Another position is that these methods do not work. Either there are practical issues (to actually sleep and rejuvenate, your body needs time to pass) or Supernal limitations doing this. Somewhere in the source code of magic there is a line saying: &quot;Serial Murder is the only path to immortality.&quot; The only true ways of prolonging your life beyond a normal lifespan are, to put it lightly, ethically questionable. They involve soul theft, life force theft, etc. The other stuff just does not work. <br /> <br /> The primary argument here, I think, is thematic. If all these other ways work, then it weakens the theme of life extension being an unnatural and arrogant action. Therefore they do not work. If you want to live forever or just for a very very long time, be a Tremere and be a monster.<br /> <br /> A third position and the one I espouse is to do a bit of houseruling and link wisdom to extending one's life. It works and it has few real drawbacks, but eventually your wisdom will start dropping from it. Since very long-lived mages tend to end up insane and a danger to all around them (low wisdom = more paradox in general) there is a strong incentive to not extend one's lifespan too much and accept that you have to move on some day. This is part of mage culture and is to some degree enforced by both the Pentacle and the Seers. Tremere are hunted, 200 year old mages are politely asked to move on (then less politely, then helped along), etc.<br /> <br /> I think my arguments boil down to firstly verisimilitude (a fraught word on the best of days): it just makes sense to me, without introducing Supernal limitations or hindering, what I see as, extrapolation from the magic rules and practices. Another argument is thematic: I like Wisdom being a weapon of the Exarchs to reinforce the prison, a gift from the Oracles to weaken the seers and a consequence of reality interacting with the abyss.<br /> <br /> None of the three positions have anything against mages being spry and active at the age of 110, or the average, natural lifespan of mages being well above the normal human one. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T15:16:44-07:00","id":113585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=48074#post48074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue isn't some Catholic analogy. The issue is that the Path of Death is actually the Path of Transformation - Moros specialise in the Supernal resonance of transition between fixed states. The Path has always been portrayed as being curiously not-at-all morbid. Death, to the main researchers into it in Mage's universe, is a spiritual transition which isn't something to fear or put off forever. Delay, sure, but everything dies eventually. In-setting, the fear of death, and the related fear that only an elect few get to the afterlife <u>is one of the Exarchs</u>.<br /> <br /> Tremere believe differently, but they've had their spiritual nature dipped into the Abyss as part of their recruitment - they're a corrupted form of the Moros.<br /> <br /> Do other mages fear death and seek immortality? A few, but predominantly members of other Paths. The Pentacle takes the majority Moros lead because that's how Pentacle society works. The Silver Ladder know that morbid fear is one of the Enemy, and think that Ascension is preferable to lichdom (and that most lichdom methods corrupt the soul, so preclude Ascension). The further a group gets from the meritocratic &quot;listen to the experts&quot; core of mage society, the more accepting it is of fringe ideas like making your stay in the Fallen World permanent.<br /> <br /> Death Archmasters are, thanks to the way Archmastery works, mostly either ex-Moros or mages who had Death as a third Ruling Arcanum through their Legacy. The characters with the greatest ability to seek immortality methods are the ones with the least inclination to do it.<br /> <br /> Exceptions exist, and when we're talking about Masters and archmasters everyone's an exceptional individual, but they're on the fringes because a fifth of the Awakened - the important fifth to the subject - mostly reject immortality as a philosophy and decry it as a spiritually poisionous dead-end. That most liches <i>are</i> Mad, bad, or dangerous to know just reinforces that societal stereotype.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I never really understood this, death is something uncertain, terrifying in the World of Darkness and fear of death is treated as a sign of spiritual degeneration.<br /> The archmasters (moros or not) do everything to not die (even if they do not have a lot of effort to do to get there; after becoming archmaster they completely reject Death), but mages who have the same attitudes are unlikely to become archmasters; odd by not doing filthy things like Lichdom to not die; by the simple fact to being scared by death.<br /> I find this a bit hypocritical*; especially since only conformity to dogma really justified belief in a possible reincarnation in the view of the Travelers.<br /> (what they can see is very pessimisticn how members of Orders justify the number of Deaths in the Underwolrd, okey this is not something that happens every day, but justify reincarnation so long as see crowds in the Underworld is not that hard ?)<br /> Okay, fear about no lives after Death is a Exarch; but a eternity in the Underworld is not really better than the cessation of existence. (certain for the Sleepers and probaly too for the Awakens)<br /> <br /> And that finally the souls sink forever the Underworld; only sometimes hampered for some time by their ghosts (a ghost is just a echo but the true self, soul, is apparently stuck forever anyway); shows that despair is the most logical attitude.<br /> <br /> <br /> (The Owod was already sad with the possibility of a real life after death (regardless reach distant shores, most have disintegrated in the Oblivion) and mages are not reincarnated; it would be surprising if nwod mages have an automatic ticket to reincarnation.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mages are apparently the guys who won the lottery; but just to earn a tiny chance to escape death by archmastery (and yet it is even more to won the lottery a second time through a personal effort).; and it is a little strange that the best and most likely happen is to act as if this was not the case then act completely the opposite way once become archmaster.<br /> <br /> I mean, what can a traveler than to try to move forward and have the foolish hope of becoming archmaster ? (and become a tremere at the very end of his life, if he has failed; this still better than the Underworld) do not see why &quot;accept&quot; death (why &quot;accept&quot; nothingness after death ? you must lives with this but you don't &quot;accept&quot;) or how quiet due to pure beliefs about reincarnation is healthier than uncertainty or fear. (but there is a difference between being afraid of death and become a tremere; but I think not that being reasonably afraid death is worse than waste his time and not invest entirely itself in his quest because there will be other chances to reach the Ascension after this life); it's clear that a traveler have only one chance.<br /> <br /> <br /> *I think overall that archmasters act in a way which would deprive a traveler of any chance of becoming archmasters if he act in the same way; it makes you wonder how they became archmasters in first time. (But I think the aspect of &quot;Who can become archmaster and why it rather than another&quot; is a weak point of the Imperial Mysteries; it is difficult to justify getting the Quintessence without making it completely random or so easy that one wonders why there is little archmasters and feel that those who are have done nothing special and are not better after; I'm not saying that many official NPC are worthy to be archmasters; but it is easy for player to create a character that is as much as officials archmasters examples)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","user":"Suleri Drals","date":". 04-16-2014, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T17:50:39-07:00","id":113689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-