"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=114164#post114164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a one-shot in one of the books that involves something not unlike that, except there it's a spirit with... reincarnation numina I think was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it's at the end of Boston Unvieled. (Except it doesn't just extend your life, it *resurrects* it... so does that restart your karmic lifespan or what?) On that note, wouldn't it be feasible (certainly not easy) for someone suitably versed in spirit lore to be granted immortality by a high ranking spirit? I think it was mentioned somewhere (GMC?) that even a rank 5 could do something on that magnitude.<br /> <br /> How would that be viewed in the awakened community? Would being so tied to the fallen world's shadow endanger a mage's chance at ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2583-amikaligula","name":"amikaligula","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T23:28:49-07:00","id":114578,"title":"","content":"Suleri your argument is flawed on a very central point. Ghosts are not people. Hyperbole aside, Ghosthood and the Underworld are obviously not the afterlife, for one thing not everyone leaves behind a ghost, it's somewhat rare. Secondly, ghosts are clearly not human souls, any Disciple of Death can see both and tell the difference between them. This is why mages have no problem with treating ghosts with the same discourtesies they'd offer to spirits of the Shadow, because from the Mage perspective the major difference between ghosts and such spirits is a ghost's irritating pretense of humanity. What exactly ghosts are is not explained, the Death aspect of a soul torn free by unfinished business? A shadow cast in Twilight by the resonance of a person's passing? I dunno, don't think mages do either really, but there's a number of things they aren't and a human soul is one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T01:26:26-07:00","id":114605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SirPants</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=114578#post114578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suleri your argument is flawed on a very central point. Ghosts are not people. Hyperbole aside, Ghosthood and the Underworld are obviously not the afterlife, for one thing not everyone leaves behind a ghost, it's somewhat rare. Secondly, ghosts are clearly not human souls, any Disciple of Death can see both and tell the difference between them. This is why mages have no problem with treating ghosts with the same discourtesies they'd offer to spirits of the Shadow, because from the Mage perspective the major difference between ghosts and such spirits is a ghost's irritating pretense of humanity. What exactly ghosts are is not explained, the Death aspect of a soul torn free by unfinished business? A shadow cast in Twilight by the resonance of a person's passing? I dunno, don't think mages do either really, but there's a number of things they aren't and a human soul is one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not now official that the soul languishing somewhere in the Underworld when his ghost is in the Twillight; but reflowed with the soul if the ghost down in the Underworld ? (That is why the ghosts of the Underworld often become more aware)<br /> And the fact that &quot;the beings inhabiting the Underworld and vaguely resembling ghosts of Twillight&quot; are much more numerous than the ghosts of Twillight, so many that they would not be surprising that all humans go there.<br /> <br /> And how the process of the Fallen World seem to really work shows that souls never go Stygia (The ideas of reincarnation that many mages have are not based on much; It's a pure ideology, as the Empyrean seen by the Silver Ladder only for the religious mages; The archmasters who have much more knowledge rather tend to think that the current souls do not return to the system but are replaced by the mysterious Principle); it is only a model of the process of death is supposed dictated how the Fallen World is supposed to behave; here certainly the Underworld had this feature.<br /> And how the Underworld is now, it is unlikely that it still works.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","user":"Suleri Drals","date":". 04-17-2014, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T02:45:03-07:00","id":114627,"title":"","content":"Atlantean orthodoxy says that ghosts aren't people. However, the truth isn't really clear.<br /> <br /> Ghosts don't seem to have souls... but then you can rip out a persons soul and replace it with another so the exact relationship between a person and their soul is at best complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T05:18:36-07:00","id":114663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/42904-what-are-the-options-for-mages-not-dying-of-old-age?p=114627#post114627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atlantean orthodoxy says that ghosts aren't people. However, the truth isn't really clear.<br /> <br /> Ghosts don't seem to have souls... but then you can rip out a persons soul and replace it with another so the exact relationship between a person and their soul is at best complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts of Twilight are only echoes, but after that I understood; it is likely that the true soul is in the Underworld all along. (and eventually merge if the ghost going in the Underworld)<br /> A ghost that has no anchors will not form and will not in the Underworld (Or a ghost who solves his anchors will disappear); but there is nothing to say that the true soul out so far. (Everything I found on this notion is not really going in the direction that the true soul can go out or that the souls of those who have never had a ghost aren't in the Underworld)<br /> <br /> The soul does not seem indivisible; when someone &quot;loses his soul&quot; it is probably just a part. (The part that corresponds to &quot;Death&quot; or &quot;Prime&quot; as appropriate); A mage who has lost his soul; at least keep the &quot;Mind&quot;. (Although it is likely that further lose its ability to do magic, ect ... each part is important to the overall operation, eg a Morphean can learn more probably because the lack of &quot;Death &quot;makes too static*)<br /> <br /> *The part of the soul that can die seems bound to change; this is probably why the Legacys as the Tremere &quot;link at Fallen World&quot; and prevents the necessary change to Ascension.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T06:18:07-07:00","id":114679,"title":"","content":"There's a book on the Underworld. No mention of a realm where the real souls go.<br /> <br /> That said, it's pretty focused on Sin-Eaters, for whom ghosts are exactly what they claim to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T15:26:44-07:00","id":114976,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the most likely reason there aren't hundreds of immortal mages is because those that are powerful enough to seek immortality are powerful enough to try to become archmasters. Those that succede gain effective immortality, those that fail are unexisted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T16:02:42-07:00","id":115003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originall